**Avoid stale pollers clearing a newer job marker.**

`setActiveJob( sessionId, jobId )` can overwrite the same session with a newer job, but any older poller exit still calls `clearActiveJob( sessionId )` and deletes that newer marker. Pass `jobId` through cleanup and only clear when the stored value still matches.



<details>
<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-					clearActiveJob( sessionId );
+					clearActiveJob( sessionId, jobId );
@@
-							clearActiveJob( sessionId );
+							clearActiveJob( sessionId, jobId );
@@
-						clearActiveJob( sessionId );
+						clearActiveJob( sessionId, jobId );
@@
-				clearActiveJob( sessionId );
+				clearActiveJob( sessionId, jobId );
```

And update the utility accordingly:

```diff
-export function clearActiveJob( sessionId ) {
+export function clearActiveJob( sessionId, jobId ) {
 	try {
 		const raw = sessionStorage.getItem( STORAGE_KEY );
 		if ( ! raw ) {
 			return;
 		}
 		const jobs = JSON.parse( raw );
+		if ( jobs[ sessionId ] !== jobId ) {
+			return;
+		}
 		delete jobs[ sessionId ];
```

