_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Restore multisite context only after all attachment operations finish.**

When `switch_to_blog()` is used, `media_handle_sideload()` creates the attachment on the target blog, but Lines 310-312 restore before `update_post_meta()` and `wp_get_attachment_url()`. Those calls can then run against the original blog with the target blog’s attachment ID.



<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 		$attachment_id = media_handle_sideload( $file_array, $post_id, $title );

-		if ( $switched ) {
-			restore_current_blog();
-		}
-
 		if ( is_wp_error( $attachment_id ) ) {
+			if ( $switched ) {
+				restore_current_blog();
+			}
+
 			if ( file_exists( $tmp_file ) ) {
 				unlink( $tmp_file ); // phpcs:ignore WordPress.WP.AlternativeFunctions.unlink_unlink
 			}

 			return $attachment_id;
 		}

 		// Set alt text from keyword.
 		update_post_meta( $attachment_id, '_wp_attachment_image_alt', $title );

 		$attachment_url = wp_get_attachment_url( $attachment_id );
+
+		if ( $switched ) {
+			restore_current_blog();
+		}
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@includes/Abilities/ImageSources/ImageSourceFactory.php` around lines 308 -
325, The multisite context is being restored too early: after calling
media_handle_sideload($file_array, $post_id, $title) the code calls
restore_current_blog() before performing update_post_meta($attachment_id,
'_wp_attachment_image_alt', $title) and wp_get_attachment_url($attachment_id),
