_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**`fullPage` capture mutates the user's actual scroll position.**

In `capture-screenshot`, `scrollToRevealLazyContent( window, document, … )` (line 209) drives the live document through every `SCROLL_STEP` and finishes by parking the page at `scrollY = 0` (see lines 158–161 of the helper). If the user was reading mid-page when the agent invoked this ability, they're snapped to the top with a visible scroll-jank pass first. Capture an explicit "before" position and restore it after the lazy-load pass.



<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 		if ( fullPage && target === document.body ) {
 			const rawHeight = document.documentElement.scrollHeight;
 			captureHeight = Math.min( rawHeight, MAX_CAPTURE_HEIGHT );
 			truncated = rawHeight > MAX_CAPTURE_HEIGHT;

