+			const originalScrollX = window.scrollX;
+			const originalScrollY = window.scrollY;
+			try {
+				await scrollToRevealLazyContent( window, document, captureHeight );
+			} finally {
+				window.scrollTo( originalScrollX, originalScrollY );
+			}
 		}
```

For `screenshot-url` this isn't a concern (the iframe is throwaway), so no change is needed there.
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@src/abilities/screenshot.js` around lines 199 - 210, When doing a fullPage
capture in capture-screenshot (the block that computes captureHeight/truncated
and calls scrollToRevealLazyContent), save the current scroll position (e.g.,
window.scrollY or document.documentElement.scrollTop) before calling
scrollToRevealLazyContent and restore it after the awaited call completes so the
user's viewport is returned to the original position; only apply this when
target === document.body (no change needed for iframe/`screenshot-url`). Ensure
the restore happens after the await and handles async exceptions (restore in
finally) so the page isn't left scrolled if scrollToRevealLazyContent throws.
```

