body:
_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**A11y: edit/delete actions stay at `opacity: 0.35` for keyboard users.**

The actions are only brought to full opacity on `.gratis-ai-agent-card:hover`, so users who tab to the Edit/Delete buttons via keyboard will see them at 35% — both unclear visually and likely failing WCAG non-text contrast on the icon glyphs. Reveal on focus too.

<details>
<summary>♿ Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 .gratis-ai-agent-card:hover .gratis-ai-agent-card-actions {
 	opacity: 1;
 }
+
+.gratis-ai-agent-card:focus-within .gratis-ai-agent-card-actions,
+.gratis-ai-agent-card-actions:focus-within {
+	opacity: 1;
+}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
.gratis-ai-agent-card-actions {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	gap: 2px;

	/* Subtly hidden; revealed fully on card hover. */
	opacity: 0.35;
	transition: opacity 120ms;
}

.gratis-ai-agent-card:hover .gratis-ai-agent-card-actions {
	opacity: 1;
}

.gratis-ai-agent-card:focus-within .gratis-ai-agent-card-actions,
.gratis-ai-agent-card-actions:focus-within {
	opacity: 1;
}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@src/settings-page/style.css` around lines 885 - 897, The action buttons
(.gratis-ai-agent-card-actions) remain at opacity:0.35 for keyboard users
because the reveal only triggers on .gratis-ai-agent-card:hover; update the CSS
to also reveal actions when the card or its actions receive keyboard focus
(e.g., add selectors for .gratis-ai-agent-card:focus-within
.gratis-ai-agent-card-actions and .gratis-ai-agent-card-actions:focus-visible)
so Edit/Delete icons go to full opacity for keyboard navigation while keeping
the same transition timing.
```

</details>

