_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**AI fallback failure discards the aggregated free-source context.**

When `no_generate_fallback` is falsy and AI generation is attempted at line 285, a failure inside the recursive `'generate'` branch returns the AI `WP_Error` directly — the `$tried` map of free-source failures is never surfaced to the caller. So if both `pixabay` and the AI provider fail, the user only sees the AI error and has no signal that pixabay was tried (or why it failed).

Consider merging the AI failure into the aggregated `all_sources_failed` message, or at minimum recording it into `$tried` before falling through to the error builder.



