_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Reject non-attachment IDs here.**

`get_post()` accepts any post type. A page/post ID can slip through and be stored as `custom_logo`, which leaves theme state pointing at something that is not a media asset. This should require an image attachment.


<details>
<summary>🧱 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-		if ( ! get_post( $attachment_id ) ) {
+		$post = get_post( $attachment_id );
+		$mime = (string) get_post_mime_type( $attachment_id );
+
+		if (
+			! $post
+			|| 'attachment' !== $post->post_type
+			|| ! str_starts_with( $mime, 'image/' )
+		) {
 			return new WP_Error(
 				'invalid_attachment_id',
-				__( 'Attachment not found.', 'superdav-ai-agent' )
+				__( 'attachment_id must reference an image attachment.', 'superdav-ai-agent' )
 			);
 		}

 		// Set the custom_logo theme mod — the standard WordPress site-logo mechanism.
 		set_theme_mod( 'custom_logo', $attachment_id );

 		// Also wire as site icon when the attachment is an SVG (modern browsers support SVG favicons).
-		$mime = (string) get_post_mime_type( $attachment_id );
 		if ( 'image/svg+xml' === $mime ) {
 			update_option( 'site_icon', $attachment_id );
 		}
```
</details>

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@includes/Abilities/GenerateLogoSvgAbility.php` around lines 314 - 327, The
code currently accepts any post ID; restrict it to an image attachment by first
verifying get_post( $attachment_id ) returns a post with post_type ===
'attachment' and then confirming it's an image (use wp_attachment_is_image(
$attachment_id ) or check get_post_mime_type starts with 'image/'); if either
check fails return a WP_Error (e.g. 'invalid_attachment_id' or
'invalid_attachment_type') before calling set_theme_mod( 'custom_logo',
$attachment_id ) so only media attachments are stored as the custom logo (keep
the existing SVG-specific site_icon update).
```

</details>

