**Unknown-field-only payloads can still mutate rows via `updated_at` (nondeterministic affected-row count).**

Line 177 always injects `updated_at` before checking whether any caller-provided field survived allowlisting. That makes “unknown fields only” requests sometimes update 1 row (time tick) and sometimes 0 (same second), which breaks deterministic no-op semantics.



<details>
<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
 		$table              = Database::table_name();
-		$data['updated_at'] = current_time( 'mysql', true );
