_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Clear legacy cron hooks on upgrade and deactivation.**

Lines 34-39 and 139-142 only manage `sd_ai_agent_reindex`. On upgraded sites, any existing `wp_ai_agent_reindex` / `wp_sd_ai_agent_reindex` events will survive forever, and this PR also removes the old cleanup path from the database layer. That leaves orphaned recurring cron rows after upgrade and even after deactivation.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
 class KnowledgeHooks {
@@
 	public static function register(): void {
+		wp_clear_scheduled_hook( 'wp_ai_agent_reindex' );
+		wp_clear_scheduled_hook( 'wp_sd_ai_agent_reindex' );
+
 		add_action( 'save_post', [ __CLASS__, 'handle_save_post' ], 20, 2 );
 		add_action( 'delete_post', [ __CLASS__, 'handle_delete_post' ], 10, 1 );
 		add_action( self::CRON_HOOK, [ __CLASS__, 'handle_cron_reindex' ] );
@@
 	public static function deactivate(): void {
-		$timestamp = wp_next_scheduled( self::CRON_HOOK );
-		if ( $timestamp ) {
-			wp_unschedule_event( $timestamp, self::CRON_HOOK );
-		}
+		wp_clear_scheduled_hook( self::CRON_HOOK );
+		wp_clear_scheduled_hook( 'wp_ai_agent_reindex' );
+		wp_clear_scheduled_hook( 'wp_sd_ai_agent_reindex' );
 	}
 }
```

</details>

Please mirror the same legacy cleanup in `uninstall.php` and add a regression test that pre-schedules the old hook names before `register()`/`deactivate()`.  



Also applies to: 139-142

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the
rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.

In `@includes/Knowledge/KnowledgeHooks.php` around lines 34 - 39, Update
KnowledgeHooks to remove legacy cron hook names ('wp_ai_agent_reindex' and
'wp_sd_ai_agent_reindex') wherever you schedule/clear cron events: in
KnowledgeHooks::register() (near add_action/self::CRON_HOOK scheduling) add
wp_clear_scheduled_hook('wp_ai_agent_reindex') and
wp_clear_scheduled_hook('wp_sd_ai_agent_reindex') so any old recurring events
are removed on upgrade/registration; mirror the same clears in the deactivation
path (the method that clears self::CRON_HOOK around lines where
handle_cron_reindex is unregistered) and also add the same two
wp_clear_scheduled_hook calls to uninstall.php; finally add a regression test
that pre-schedules 'wp_ai_agent_reindex' and 'wp_sd_ai_agent_reindex' before
calling KnowledgeHooks::register() and before calling the deactivate routine,
then assert those hooks are no longer scheduled after the call.
```

</details>

