_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Inline `affected` check diverges from the tested `hasLiveSiteChangeActivity` helper.**

This effect uses `onboardingJob.toolCalls?.some( ( entry ) => entry?.response?.affected )`, which is weaker than the helper it duplicates: the helper additionally requires `entry?.type === 'response'` and `typeof entry.response.affected === 'object'`. So the unit-tested contract is not what runs here, and a non-response entry that happens to carry an `affected` field would trigger build mode. Reuse the helper to keep behavior and tests aligned.



<details>
<summary>♻️ Suggested change</summary>

```diff
+import { hasLiveSiteChangeActivity } from './frontend-onboarding';
```

```diff
-		if (
-			! onboardingJob.toolCalls?.some(
-				( entry ) => entry?.response?.affected
-			)
-		) {
+		if ( ! hasLiveSiteChangeActivity( onboardingJob.toolCalls ) ) {
 			return;
 		}
```
</details>

Separately, note the centered `intro` panel only resets when it has already advanced to `building` (Line 150). If the session ends without ever emitting an `affected` response, the widget stays locked in centered intro mode (drag/resize disabled) indefinitely — worth confirming that's acceptable.

